<title>HUNGARY: Hungary three-month bill yield rises to 22.51 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary three-month bill yield rises to 22.51 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of three-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 22.51 percent, up from 22.38 percent at an auction one week ago, the National Bank of Hungary said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received	4,885.01 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    4,885.01 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    22.51 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     94.6861 pct</p>
</text>
